# "A 5 Minute introduction to StoryCAD" (YouTube qFpTI15-q7A, 2023) as a script (#1421 Milestone 4).
# Test profile: a regression check of the steps the video shows.
# Presentation profile: drives the app for an OBS recording; narrate lines become the .srt captions.
#   StoryCADAutomation run StoryCADTests/AutomationScripts/Intro-Video.scs
# Left out of the video's steps: the user manual (opens a browser), the Windows print preview,
# and the Scrivener export (needs Scrivener). The narration mentions them over the app.
script "Intro Video"

step "The main window"
launch
expect FileOpenNav exists
narrate "StoryCAD is a free and open source computer-aided design tool for fiction writers."
click SampleOutlinesNavItem
select FileOpenSamplesList "The Old Man and the Sea"
click PrimaryButton                       # "Open"
expect tree contains "The Old Man and the Sea"
narrate "On the left is the navigation pane. It shows every element of your outline as a tree."
open-node tree "The Old Man and the Sea/Characters/Santiago"
narrate "The right side is the content pane. It shows the element you select in the tree."
pause 2
narrate "The menu bar at the top opens files, adds story elements, runs tools and prints reports."
click PreferencesButton
narrate "Preferences hold your name, your folders and how StoryCAD saves your work."
pause 2
dialog "Preferences" click name:"Cancel"

step "A new outline"
menu OpenCreateFileMenuItem
click CreateNewOutlineNavItem
narrate "StoryCAD creates new outlines from templates. This one starts from the blank template."
set FileOpenProjectNameTextBox "Fish Story"
press "Tab"                               # the name binding updates only when focus leaves the box
click PrimaryButton                       # "Create outline"
expect tree contains "Fish Story"
narrate "A blank outline has two nodes: the story overview and the trash can."
pause 2

step "The story overview"
narrate "The overview is the root of the tree and the place to start."
tab StoryIdeaTab
focus StoryIdeaRichEdit                  # RichEdit boxes have no Value pattern, so focus and type
type "Codify a local urban legend as a morality tale."
narrate "Each element has tabs. Each tab covers one part of that element."
tab ConceptTab
focus ConceptRichEdit
type "What if a morally upstanding man failed utterly and repeatedly?"
pause 2

step "Story elements"
narrate "You build your outline by adding story elements: problems, characters, settings and scenes."
context-menu tree "Fish Story" "Add Elements/Add Problem"
open-node tree "Fish Story/New Problem"
set ProblemNameTextBox "An old man hasn't caught a fish in 84 days"
expect tree contains "Fish Story/An old man hasn't caught a fish in 84 days"
click tree "Fish Story"                   # the root row has no Invoke; click falls back to a real pointer
menu AddCharacterMenuItem
open-node tree "Fish Story/New Character"
set CharacterNameTextBox "Santiago"
click tree "Fish Story"                   # the root row has no Invoke; click falls back to a real pointer
menu AddCharacterMenuItem
open-node tree "Fish Story/New Character"
set CharacterNameTextBox "Manolin"
expect tree contains "Fish Story/Santiago"
expect tree contains "Fish Story/Manolin"
narrate "Add elements in any order, as inspiration strikes or from start to finish."
pause 2

step "Plotting aids"
narrate "StoryCAD has tools for plotting. Master Plots adds a ready-made story structure."
click tree "Fish Story"                   # the root row has no Invoke; click falls back to a real pointer
menu MasterPlotsMenuItem
select MasterPlotsCombo "Ascent/Descent"   # the 2023 video used Seven Point Story Structure, now a beat sheet
pause 2
click PrimaryButton                       # "Copy"
expect StatusMessageText text "MasterPlot Ascent/Descent inserted"
expect tree contains "Fish Story/Rise and Fall"   # one of the three scenes it inserts
pause 2

step "Reports"
narrate "When it is time to write, print reports from your outline."
menu PrintReportsMenuItem
toggle PrintReportsOverviewCheck on
tab PrintReportsCharactersTab
toggle PrintReportsCharacterListCheck on
pause 2
dialog "Generate Reports" click name:"Cancel"
narrate "You can also export your outline to a Scrivener project and draft from it there."
pause 2

step "Close"
narrate "StoryCAD is free from the Microsoft Store and the Mac App Store. Thanks for watching."
menu ExitMenuItem
dialog "Save changes?" click name:"No"
expect-exit
